      "writtenOn": "2022-05-31T15:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have `pair\u003cSkTileMode, SkTileMode\u003e` in several other places, and `tuple\u003cSkTileMode, SkTileMode\u003e` here. Please consider a dedicated struct with a name, like `struct TileModePair { SkTileMode tileMode[2]; }`. This will make code easier to read, as `const TileModePair\u0026 p` is easier to read than `const std::pair\u003cTileMode, TileMode\u003e\u0026 p`. It\u0027s also lighter-weight on the compiler.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "df65376df4b8f44ae0589e7efb33a5cbd9a17f42",
